WEBVTT

1
00:00:30.291 --> 00:00:32.375
<b>In the previous verse, Lord Krishna revealed</b>

2
00:00:32.375 --> 00:00:39.750
<b>that those who understand His divine </b>
<b>birth, nature, and pastimes attain Him</b>

3
00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:45.000
<b>and break free from material bondage.</b>

4
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:49.708
<b>Now, Lord Krishna elaborates</b>

5
00:00:49.708 --> 00:00:56.166
<b>on how people in the past gained </b>
<b>true knowledge and found Him. </b>

6
00:00:56.166 --> 00:00:56.958
<b>Yet,</b>

7
00:00:56.958 --> 00:01:01.583
<b>there are obstacles on this path </b>
<b>that must be overcome –</b>

8
00:01:01.583 --> 00:01:05.416
<b>these obstacles are our focus here.</b>

9
00:01:09.708 --> 00:01:11.375
<b>Krishna speaks:</b>

10
00:01:11.375 --> 00:01:15.250
<b>Those who freed themselves from attachment,</b>
<b>fear, and anger –</b>

11
00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:18.583
<b>immersing their minds completely in Me</b>

12
00:01:18.583 --> 00:01:20.958
<b>and taking refuge in My presence –</b>

13
00:01:20.958 --> 00:01:25.541
<b>have been purified through knowledge's austerity</b>

14
00:01:25.541 --> 00:01:29.875
<b>and they ultimately attained Me.</b>

15
00:01:29.875 --> 00:01:31.416
<b>This process of understanding Krishna</b>

16
00:01:31.416 --> 00:01:37.875
<b>and developing spiritual wisdom </b>
<b>is called ‘Tapasya’ -</b>

17
00:01:37.875 --> 00:01:39.708
<b>'austerity.'</b>
<b>It's not an easy path,</b>

18
00:01:39.708 --> 00:01:42.875
<b>nor is this wisdom easily gained.</b>

19
00:01:42.875 --> 00:01:51.291
<b>It demands patience, effort, </b>
<b>and most crucially, humility –</b>

20
00:01:51.291 --> 00:01:54.750
<b>the humility to acknowledge our ignorance</b>

21
00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:59.166
<b>and accept that certain truths </b>
<b>reveal themselves only in time.</b>

22
00:01:59.166 --> 00:02:03.291
<b>Just as gold emerges pure from fire,</b>

23
00:02:03.291 --> 00:02:10.000
<b>the mind emerges completely purified </b>
<b>through this rigorous spiritual practice.</b>

24
00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:10.791
<b>Yet</b>

25
00:02:10.791 --> 00:02:14.500
<b>three obstacles block this path:</b>

26
00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:18.541
<b>First - Attachment (excessive desire)</b>

27
00:02:18.541 --> 00:02:20.625
<b>Second - Fear</b>

28
00:02:20.625 --> 00:02:23.083
<b>Third - Anger</b>

29
00:02:23.083 --> 00:02:25.583
<b>Their sequence matters,</b>

30
00:02:25.583 --> 00:02:29.625
<b>as attachment births both fear and anger.</b>

31
00:02:29.625 --> 00:02:32.375
<b>Let's understand why.</b>

32
00:02:32.375 --> 00:02:38.375
<b>How does attachment or excessive </b>
<b>obsession arise?</b>

33
00:02:38.375 --> 00:02:45.041
<b>Humans become dependent on </b>
<b>others or objects for happiness.</b>

34
00:02:45.041 --> 00:02:46.416
<b>For example,</b>

35
00:02:46.416 --> 00:02:52.083
<b>"Life will be joyful only when this </b>
<b>person becomes my partner"</b>

36
00:02:52.083 --> 00:02:56.041
<b>or "when I achieve a desired </b>
<b>thing or that position."</b>

37
00:02:56.041 --> 00:03:02.291
<b>This simple desire transforms </b>
<b>into excessive attachment</b>

38
00:03:02.291 --> 00:03:06.416
<b>when one becomes enslaved to such thoughts.</b>

39
00:03:06.416 --> 00:03:14.500
<b>This attachment can be to anything </b>
<b>we deem essential for happiness – </b>

40
00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:16.000
<b>a beautiful person,</b>

41
00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:16.958
<b>position,</b>

42
00:03:16.958 --> 00:03:17.750
<b>wealth,</b>

43
00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:18.791
<b>possessions.</b>

44
00:03:18.791 --> 00:03:20.208
<b>or any such attachments.</b>

45
00:03:20.208 --> 00:03:23.916
<b>Consider how this breeds fear:</b>

46
00:03:23.916 --> 00:03:26.458
<b>"What if the person I love,</b>

47
00:03:26.458 --> 00:03:29.500
<b>rejects my proposal?",</b>

48
00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:32.750
<b>"This position that gives me respect,</b>

49
00:03:32.750 --> 00:03:35.875
<b>what if I lose this position?",</b>

50
00:03:35.875 --> 00:03:38.875
<b>"Today I live a luxurious life.</b>

51
00:03:38.875 --> 00:03:41.208
<b>What if this luxury slips away?"</b>

52
00:03:41.208 --> 00:03:42.625
<b>First comes attachment,</b>

53
00:03:42.625 --> 00:03:45.208
<b>then fear of not obtaining,</b>

54
00:03:45.208 --> 00:03:47.666
<b>and once obtained,</b>

55
00:03:47.666 --> 00:03:50.041
<b>then the fear of losing.</b>

56
00:03:50.041 --> 00:03:53.125
<b>From this same source springs anger.</b>

57
00:03:53.125 --> 00:03:54.125
<b>Think,</b>

58
00:03:54.125 --> 00:03:56.166
<b>when do we become angry?</b>

59
00:03:56.166 --> 00:04:01.916
<b>When circumstances or people threaten </b>
<b>to take what we hold dear.</b>

60
00:04:01.916 --> 00:04:05.791
<b>If someone else captures</b>
<b>your beloved's attention –</b>

61
00:04:05.791 --> 00:04:08.666
<b>anger toward that person.</b>

62
00:04:08.666 --> 00:04:14.500
<b>If you're attached to your </b>
<b>position and get removed –</b>

63
00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:16.833
<b>anger toward that superior.</b>

64
00:04:16.833 --> 00:04:21.375
<b>If your favorite show is </b>
<b>interrupted by a power cut –</b>

65
00:04:21.375 --> 00:04:25.500
<b>anger towards the electricity </b>
<b>department and the situation.</b>

66
00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:26.333
<b>Attachment,</b>

67
00:04:26.333 --> 00:04:31.375
<b>which means excessive desire, </b>
<b>births both fear and anger.</b>

68
00:04:31.375 --> 00:04:38.250
<b>Lost in these material concerns, </b>
<b>humans drift from their spiritual truth,</b>

69
00:04:38.250 --> 00:04:41.416
<b>pursuing only physical pleasures.</b>

70
00:04:41.416 --> 00:04:43.833
<b>Though aware of the body's mortality,</b>

71
00:04:43.833 --> 00:04:51.583
<b>they deny it – this stubborn denial of the </b>
<b>known truth is ignorance itself.</b>

72
00:04:51.583 --> 00:04:55.708
<b>To overcome this, spiritual </b>
<b>knowledge's austerity is essential,</b>

73
00:04:55.708 --> 00:04:59.083
<b>as is fixing the mind on Krishna,</b>

74
00:04:59.083 --> 00:05:07.875
<b>for only this liberates us from worldly</b>
<b>attachments and the bonds of mortality.</b>

75
00:05:07.875 --> 00:05:09.666
<b>And ultimately,</b>

76
00:05:09.666 --> 00:05:12.625
<b>we shall attain Krishna's divine abode,</b>

77
00:05:12.625 --> 00:05:15.125
<b>we shall attain Krishna Himself.</b>

78
00:05:19.833 --> 00:05:22.291
<b>Did you know?</b>

79
00:05:22.291 --> 00:05:30.458
<b>Many have risen above material attachments,</b>

80
00:05:30.458 --> 00:05:42.958
<b>focused on spiritual wisdom, purified themselves, </b>
<b>and ultimately attained Me.</b>

81
00:05:42.958 --> 00:05:46.625
<b>However,</b>

82
00:05:46.625 --> 00:05:49.833
<b>this is no small matter,</b>

83
00:05:49.833 --> 00:05:53.750
<b>this path isn't easy.</b>

84
00:05:53.750 --> 00:05:58.875
<b>Three major obstacles block </b>
<b>the path of spiritual knowledge:</b>

85
00:05:58.875 --> 00:06:04.000
<b>attachment (excessive desire),</b>

86
00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:05.125
<b>fear,</b>

87
00:06:05.125 --> 00:06:06.458
<b>and</b>

88
00:06:06.458 --> 00:06:08.083
<b>anger.</b>

89
00:06:08.083 --> 00:06:13.000
<b>These three bind you to this world,</b>

90
00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:16.000
<b>preventing liberation.</b>

91
00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:23.708
<b>Understand these three to protect </b>
<b>yourself from their influence.</b>

92
00:06:23.708 --> 00:06:26.625
<b>It begins with attachment</b>

93
00:06:26.625 --> 00:06:31.541
<b>– and excessive desire for any object</b>

94
00:06:31.541 --> 00:06:34.125
<b>is called Raag (attachment).</b>

95
00:06:34.125 --> 00:06:35.583
<b>Remember,</b>

96
00:06:35.583 --> 00:06:39.125
<b>attachment isn't any ordinary attraction;</b>

97
00:06:39.125 --> 00:06:48.500
<b>it arises when you become completely </b>
<b>dependent on something.</b>

98
00:06:48.500 --> 00:06:50.791
<b>For example,</b>

99
00:06:50.791 --> 00:06:53.875
<b>such intense attachment to someone</b>

100
00:06:53.875 --> 00:06:59.000
<b>that happiness seems impossible without them,</b>

101
00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:01.833
<b>nothing else brings joy.</b>

102
00:07:01.833 --> 00:07:12.125
<b>Or such attachment to position or</b>
<b>success that you forget your health and family.</b>

103
00:07:12.125 --> 00:07:20.625
<b>When despite life's comforts, you find no peace</b>

104
00:07:20.625 --> 00:07:24.583
<b>because that attachment remains unfulfilled.</b>

105
00:07:24.583 --> 00:07:32.166
<b>But does this attachment end once fulfilled?</b>

106
00:07:32.166 --> 00:07:33.958
<b>Never.</b>

107
00:07:33.958 --> 00:07:35.750
<b>Absolutely never.</b>

108
00:07:35.750 --> 00:07:40.458
<b>Now this attachment transforms into fear –</b>

109
00:07:40.458 --> 00:07:46.500
<b>fear of losing what you've gained.</b>

110
00:07:46.500 --> 00:07:47.333
<b>First,</b>

111
00:07:47.333 --> 00:07:50.500
<b>the absence of that object troubled you;</b>

112
00:07:50.500 --> 00:07:51.333
<b>now,</b>

113
00:07:51.333 --> 00:07:55.208
<b>the fear of its loss constantly haunts you.</b>

114
00:07:55.208 --> 00:07:58.916
<b>From this springs anger.</b>

115
00:07:58.916 --> 00:08:06.583
<b>Due to attachment, you want to </b>
<b>protect that object, fearful of losing it.</b>

116
00:08:06.583 --> 00:08:15.083
<b>Any person or situation that </b>
<b>threatens to separate you from it</b>

117
00:08:15.083 --> 00:08:18.375
<b>awakens both fear and anger.</b>

118
00:08:18.375 --> 00:08:20.666
<b>Consider</b>

119
00:08:20.666 --> 00:08:24.583
<b>how you're getting entangled</b>
<b>in your self-made web.</b>

120
00:08:24.583 --> 00:08:26.416
<b>This web must be cut,</b>

121
00:08:26.416 --> 00:08:28.583
<b>you must break free.</b>

122
00:08:28.583 --> 00:08:36.708
<b>Life must be viewed not through </b>
<b>material fog, but through spiritual clarity.</b>

123
00:08:36.708 --> 00:08:38.416
<b>Think:</b>

124
00:08:38.416 --> 00:08:43.833
<b>what truly matters in life?</b>

125
00:08:43.833 --> 00:08:48.000
<b>Focus your attention on spirituality.</b>

126
00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:51.458
<b>You'll realize the truth,</b>

127
00:08:51.458 --> 00:08:57.875
<b>that true joy emerges not from material objects,</b>

128
00:08:57.875 --> 00:08:58.875
<b>but</b>

129
00:08:58.875 --> 00:09:01.666
<b>from within ourselves.</b>

130
00:09:01.666 --> 00:09:08.291
<b>You'll understand that connection</b>
<b>isn't needed with the world,</b>

131
00:09:08.291 --> 00:09:09.166
<b>but</b>

132
00:09:09.166 --> 00:09:16.000
<b>with your own soul through inner reflection.</b>

133
00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:21.333
<b>When you feel unrest, fear, or anger,</b>

134
00:09:21.333 --> 00:09:25.625
<b>pause for self-reflection.</b>

135
00:09:25.625 --> 00:09:32.000
<b>Consider this sequence of </b>
<b>attachment, fear, and anger.</b>

136
00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:39.166
<b>Then ask yourself: does this situation </b>
<b>truly deserve fear or anger?</b>

137
00:09:39.166 --> 00:09:41.125
<b>When you think this way,</b>

138
00:09:41.125 --> 00:09:42.541
<b>you'll realize</b>

139
00:09:42.541 --> 00:09:49.250
<b>most situations weren't that severe.</b>

140
00:09:49.250 --> 00:09:51.958
<b>Your unrest will diminish.</b>

141
00:09:51.958 --> 00:09:54.541
<b>Progress slowly on this path,</b>

142
00:09:54.541 --> 00:09:58.041
<b>acquire spiritual knowledge.</b>

143
00:09:58.041 --> 00:09:59.250
<b>Remember,</b>

144
00:09:59.250 --> 00:10:00.750
<b>the path to liberation</b>

145
00:10:00.750 --> 00:10:09.750
<b>comes through understanding your reactions, </b>
<b>reflecting on them, and bringing inner change.</b>

146
00:10:09.750 --> 00:10:14.125
<b>This path comes through spirituality.</b>

147
00:10:14.125 --> 00:10:16.083
<b>Let us walk this path.</b>

148
00:10:20.291 --> 00:10:24.041
<b>If you've understood this verse's essence,</b>

149
00:10:24.041 --> 00:10:31.750
<b>it has the power to completely </b>
<b>transform your family and social life.</b>

150
00:10:31.750 --> 00:10:37.250
<b>This verse speaks of attachment, fear, and anger.</b>

151
00:10:37.250 --> 00:10:42.500
<b>Attachment means becoming </b>
<b>so devoted to something</b>

152
00:10:42.500 --> 00:10:46.375
<b>that you can't find joy without it.</b>

153
00:10:46.375 --> 00:10:50.291
<b>Then comes fear of not obtaining it.</b>

154
00:10:50.291 --> 00:10:56.333
<b>And if obtained, then fear of losing it.</b>

155
00:10:56.333 --> 00:10:59.375
<b>And consequently,</b>

156
00:10:59.375 --> 00:11:02.541
<b>when someone or something</b>

157
00:11:02.541 --> 00:11:12.875
<b>threatens to separate you from what you </b>
<b>treasure, it awakens anger against them.</b>

158
00:11:12.875 --> 00:11:15.083
<b>Truth is,</b>

159
00:11:15.083 --> 00:11:23.583
<b>that in most family settings, conflicts and </b>
<b>disagreements follow this pattern.</b>

160
00:11:23.583 --> 00:11:26.208
<b>The main cause isn't external –</b>

161
00:11:26.208 --> 00:11:32.208
<b>but it's your own expectations and attachments.</b>

162
00:11:32.208 --> 00:11:34.583
<b>Think of times</b>

163
00:11:34.583 --> 00:11:40.125
<b>when you felt anger toward a family member.</b>

164
00:11:40.125 --> 00:11:42.625
<b>Why did this anger arise?</b>

165
00:11:42.625 --> 00:11:45.208
<b>Was it because of their actions,</b>

166
00:11:45.208 --> 00:11:56.250
<b>or because their actions contradicted </b>
<b>your expectations?</b>

167
00:11:56.250 --> 00:11:59.416
<b>Families offer many such examples.</b>

168
00:11:59.416 --> 00:12:00.458
<b>Like</b>

169
00:12:00.458 --> 00:12:05.250
<b>when grown children choose </b>
<b>their own life partners,</b>

170
00:12:05.250 --> 00:12:13.458
<b>some parents become angry instead </b>
<b>of understanding or discussing,</b>

171
00:12:13.458 --> 00:12:17.291
<b>simply because it contradicted their expectations.</b>

172
00:12:17.291 --> 00:12:18.291
<b>Similarly,</b>

173
00:12:18.291 --> 00:12:25.375
<b>when siblings use each other's </b>
<b>belongings without asking,</b>

174
00:12:25.375 --> 00:12:33.083
<b>small matters escalate into arguments due </b>
<b>to excessive attachment to possessions.</b>

175
00:12:33.083 --> 00:12:37.791
<b>You'll find many situations where </b>
<b>anger was unnecessary.</b>

176
00:12:37.791 --> 00:12:40.166
<b>For loving relationships,</b>

177
00:12:40.166 --> 00:12:44.291
<b>reflect on your expectations and attachments.</b>

178
00:12:44.291 --> 00:12:49.041
<b>Are you imposing your expectations on others?</b>

179
00:12:49.041 --> 00:12:55.875
<b>Is your attachment to material things </b>
<b>overshadowing relationships?</b>

180
00:12:55.875 --> 00:12:58.541
<b>When you reflect, you'll realize</b>

181
00:12:58.541 --> 00:13:00.333
<b>that usually,</b>

182
00:13:00.333 --> 00:13:03.416
<b>the root of family conflicts lies not elsewhere,</b>

183
00:13:03.416 --> 00:13:04.833
<b>but</b>

184
00:13:04.833 --> 00:13:09.333
<b>in your own attachments and expectations.</b>

185
00:13:09.333 --> 00:13:17.375
<b>And this awareness will both improve </b>
<b>you and inspire change.</b>

186
00:13:21.916 --> 00:13:26.458
<b>For those who lead others in professional settings,</b>

187
00:13:26.458 --> 00:13:30.000
<b>it's crucial for them,</b>

188
00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:36.458
<b>to maintain a healthy, supportive environment.</b>

189
00:13:36.458 --> 00:13:43.791
<b>Here, viewing work through a spiritual </b>
<b>perspective is highly beneficial.</b>

190
00:13:43.791 --> 00:13:44.791
<b>Hope</b>

191
00:13:44.791 --> 00:13:52.916
<b>you've understood the sequence of attachment, </b>
<b>fear, and anger explained in this verse.</b>

192
00:13:52.916 --> 00:13:57.041
<b>This can be seen in professional settings too.</b>

193
00:13:57.041 --> 00:14:03.541
<b>Consider a senior officer so</b>
<b>attached to financial gain</b>

194
00:14:03.541 --> 00:14:10.250
<b>that they constantly fear </b>
<b>colleagues making mistakes.</b>

195
00:14:10.250 --> 00:14:11.541
<b>Consequently,</b>

196
00:14:11.541 --> 00:14:15.750
<b>not only is their personal life stressful,</b>

197
00:14:15.750 --> 00:14:16.833
<b>but</b>

198
00:14:16.833 --> 00:14:22.958
<b>this fear prevents them from trusting colleagues.</b>

199
00:14:22.958 --> 00:14:28.666
<b>They become angry at minor errors.</b>

200
00:14:28.666 --> 00:14:34.875
<b>This creates a negative work environment,</b>

201
00:14:34.875 --> 00:14:39.916
<b>which further increases stress.</b>

202
00:14:39.916 --> 00:14:41.958
<b>It becomes a cycle.</b>

203
00:14:41.958 --> 00:14:45.833
<b>And it all began from where?</b>

204
00:14:45.833 --> 00:14:50.625
<b>Yes, with harmful attachment to profit.</b>

205
00:14:50.625 --> 00:14:51.541
<b>But</b>

206
00:14:51.541 --> 00:14:56.250
<b>an officer who views this spiritually</b>

207
00:14:56.250 --> 00:14:58.000
<b>understands that</b>

208
00:14:58.000 --> 00:15:01.791
<b>if people remain true to their work,</b>

209
00:15:01.791 --> 00:15:04.708
<b>profit follows naturally.</b>

210
00:15:04.708 --> 00:15:08.458
<b>Instead of wasting time worrying about profit,</b>

211
00:15:08.458 --> 00:15:14.125
<b>they spend time training and encouraging people.</b>

212
00:15:14.125 --> 00:15:26.458
<b>They respect others as spiritual equals, </b>
<b>help them, and consequently, profit follows.</b>

213
00:15:26.458 --> 00:15:27.625
<b>Remember,</b>

214
00:15:27.625 --> 00:15:32.083
<b>professional goals are achieved </b>
<b>through colleagues.</b>

215
00:15:32.083 --> 00:15:39.625
<b>Adopt a spiritual perspective, respect all, </b>
<b>don't be attached to goals,</b>

216
00:15:39.625 --> 00:15:40.458
<b>because</b>

217
00:15:40.458 --> 00:15:43.833
<b>if people remain encouraged and trained,</b>

218
00:15:43.833 --> 00:15:47.250
<b>goals will be achieved naturally.</b>

219
00:15:47.250 --> 00:15:49.166
<b>Think about it.</b>

220
00:15:49.166 --> 00:15:51.083
